cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  A kernel-checked symmetric-square structure theorem for Cooper's sporadic
  Apéry-like operators, and the monodromy lattice of the s₇ family
message: >-
  If you use this work, cite the concept DOI below, which always resolves to the
  latest version. Please cite claims at the tier they carry: the Lean results are
  Tier A (kernel-checked), the identification of the monodromy lattice is Tier B
  (rests on a numerical computation), and no physical observable exists anywhere
  in this program. See README.md §"What you may cite, and what you may not".
type: software
