    description: Concept DOI — always resolves to the latest version
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/xaviercallens/SocrateAI-DualScaleTopologicalUniverseModel-LeanProposal
abstract: >-
  Stream 1 of the Dual-Scale Topological Universe Model: a Lean 4 formalization
  proving that the order-3 Picard–Fuchs operators of Cooper's sporadic
  Apéry-like sequences are symmetric squares of order-2 operators, uniformly in
  the template parameters; that 4 divides s₇(n), retiring the development's last
  load-bearing literature axiom; and, for the s₇ family, the rank-22 embedding
  of U ⊕ ⟨14⟩ into the K3 lattice U³ ⊕ E₈(−1)². All results are kernel-checked
  with Lean's three standard axioms and no `sorry`. The accompanying manuscript
  documents, in §9.7, a class of defect that passes every gate — a theorem that
  is true and compiles while proving less than its name says.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - Apéry-like sequences
  - Picard–Fuchs operators
  - symmetric square
  - K3 lattice
  - modular forms
